At 2-4 lb the box does NOT own mode 1 -- the fundamental (14-15 Hz) is the VALVE assembly; box KE in mode 1 is only ~0.13-0.16. So f1 shifts just ~1 Hz (14.75->14.06) across the whole 2-4 lb prior and is partly confounded with valve mass. The box's OWN energy is smeared across a veering 17-45 Hz cluster (no single clean peak). => the tap test will resolve box mass only WEAKLY from f1; the next card should use the 17-45 Hz cluster (and ideally a sensor ON the box) to update it, and expect box-mass vs valve-mass confounding.
